.TH AVR\-REPO\-MIRROR\-DISABLE 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-mirror-disable \- Stop mirroring the repository into avrea-git.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo mirror disable
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop mirroring the repository into avrea-git.
.PP
Placements are kept but become inert, so re-enabling restores them. Requires the organization admin role.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo mirror disable
    avr repo mirror disable --repo acme/widgets --yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    enabled, full_name, placements, repository_id
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-clusters (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-enable (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-place (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-status (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-unplace (1)
